    <section class="group local">
      <h2 class="ghead">LOCAL <span class="gsub">Colorado &middot; start here, the pool is one state not fifty</span><span class="gcount">11</span></h2>

      <details class="card local">
        <summary class="cardtop">
          <span class="srow"><span class="tag rank">#1</span><span class="stars" aria-label="Five out of five stars">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span><span class="tag tag-new">New 27 Aug</span></span>
          <h3 class="jt">User Experience Researcher, AI-Augmented Research</h3>
          <span class="sub"><b>Nelnet</b> &middot; Centennial, Colorado, hybrid, 24 hours a week in office &middot; $100,000 plus depending on experience &middot; req R22931</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="body">
          <ul>
          <li>Run UX research on the products of a student-loan servicing and education-payments company: study design, interviews, usability sessions, findings that product teams act on.</li>
          <li>The second half of the job is building the research practice itself with AI, including agents and automated workflows that speed up recruiting, analysis and synthesis.</li>
          <li>Hybrid team in Centennial, three days a week onsite, sitting next to product managers and designers.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="why"><b>Strong:</b> the education line accepts equivalent experience and you hold both the M.Ed. in educational technology and the BFA. The research bar is met by the ARC ten-college usability study, three personas, a 46-task taxonomy, a twelve-walkthrough method pilot and Nielsen severity ratings with a second rater, and before that by the usability studies you ran as Product Manager at ProQuest XanEdu. The AI half of the job is on the CV as built work, not interest: multi-agent orchestration, demographic-grounded synthetic-user agents for usability testing, golden-set regression checks and drift monitoring.</p>
          <p class="why"><b>Light:</b> their frame is commercial product research measured in product impact, and yours has been institutional. No stated minimum is missed, so lead with method and sample size and the frame stops mattering.</p>
          <div class="foot"><span class="tool">Lead with: the ARC ten-college usability study</span><a class="apply" href="https://nelnet.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/MyNelnet/job/Madison-WI/User-Experience-Researcher--AI-Augmented-Research_R22931" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apply &rarr;</a></div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="card local">
